      "worked_solution": "Let's add $y=\\sin x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/e32c75ac5354a826e5f357746146ca952bf2c598e426b34dffe030b09f9a1a24.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y = \\sin x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $1$ unit **down**.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y = \\sin{x} - 1.$",
